/**
 * @defgroup RoModular_Governance_AIAgents AI Agent Instructions
 * @ingroup RoModular_Governance
 * @brief How AI coding agents are instructed when working in a RoModular repository.
 *
 * Every repository carries a short root `AGENTS.md` with its project-specific
 * facts: purpose, supported build and test entry points, compatibility rules,
 * and repository boundaries. Codex and other tools that read `AGENTS.md`
 * discover it automatically.
 *
 * Each `AGENTS.md` is self-contained. No repository depends on an external
 * guidance repository, sibling checkout, or installed agent configuration to
 * clone, build, test, install, package, or be understood. Personal agent
 * preferences belong in each developer's own tool configuration, not in the
 * repositories.
 *
 * Durable project knowledge, such as architecture, plans, and design decisions,
 * lives in each repository's documentation, not in agent instructions or
 * conversation history.
 */
